        "content": "SECTION 3 — NURSE SALARY ACROSS 10 COUNTRIES (flagship)\nHeading: What do nurses earn abroad?\nIntro: Below is an illustrative comparison of indicative average annual salaries for\nregistered nurses (approx., in USD) across ten countries. Use it to explore possibilities — not\nas a promise.\n ⚠️ BANNER (must appear above table): Figures are illustrative & approximate, for\n qualified, licensed/registered nurses. They vary widely by experience, city, employer,\n shift type, currency and year. Earning these requires meeting each country's nursing-\n registration, English, and immigration requirements. Verify with official sources before\n relying on them.\n\n Country Indicative average nurse salary (USD/yr, approx.)\n\n 🇺🇸 USA ~$85,000\n\n 🇨🇦 Canada ~$70,000\n\n 🇦🇺 Australia ~$65,000\n\n 🇳🇴 Norway ~$60,000\n\n 🇩🇰 Denmark ~$58,000\n\n 🇮🇪 Ireland ~$50,000\n\n 🇩🇪 Germany ~$50,000\n\n 🇳🇱 Netherlands ~$48,000\n\n 🇬🇧 UK ~$45,000\n\n 🇸🇪 Sweden ~$45,000\n\n\n\n Dev/content instructions: Replace every figure with a verified, dated number from a\n credible source (e.g., official labour-statistics bodies, national health-service pay scales,\n OECD) and add a \"Source & year\" line. Keep one currency (USD) for fair comparison;\n consider a local-currency toggle. Keep figures consistent with the Home page salary\n table. Keep the ⚠️ banner visible.\nHonest framing (below table):\n These are possibilities for registered nurses, not guarantees. To work in these countries\n you'll typically need to clear a registration/licensing exam (e.g., NCLEX for the\n USA/Canada; CBT & OSCE for the UK NMC) and an English test (IELTS/OET), plus\n meet visa rules. That's exactly where Medico Yatra helps.\nCTA: Plan my nursing career abroad →"
