        "content": "8. FAQ (12)\n 1. Is nursing a good career for Indian students? Yes — it's one of the most in-demand,\n globally mobile healthcare careers, with strong salaries and family-settlement\n pathways in several countries.\n 2. What do nurses earn abroad? It varies widely by country, experience and employer.\n Our salary table shows illustrative averages; we share realistic, current figures in\n counselling.\n 3. Can I settle abroad with my family as a nurse? Several countries offer skilled-worker\n and dependent-visa pathways that can lead to settlement — subject to eligibility and\n current immigration rules. We guide you honestly; we don't guarantee outcomes.\n\n 4. Do I need to clear an exam to work abroad? Usually yes — e.g., NCLEX\n (USA/Canada) or UK NMC CBT + OSCE, plus an English test (IELTS/OET). We help\n you prepare.\n 5. Which country should I study nursing in? It depends on where you eventually want\n to work and settle, since registration rules differ by country. We help you choose the\n right study-abroad destination and university for your goals.\n 6. What are the eligibility requirements? Typically Class 12 with Science (PCB) +\n English and a minimum aggregate. We confirm current criteria for your chosen path.\n 7. How long does it take to become a nurse? Commonly ~3–4 years for a degree, plus\n licensing/English steps for working abroad. Timelines vary.\n 8. Is English mandatory? For most overseas registration, yes — IELTS or OET. Our sister\n brand Academic Yatra offers test prep.\n 9. Do you guarantee a job or visa abroad? No — be cautious of anyone who does. We\n provide honest, organised, end-to-end guidance to maximise your chances.\n10. Is nursing respected as a career? Globally, very much so — it's a skilled, essential\n profession with real progression into specialisation and leadership.\n11. Can my spouse work while I'm employed as a nurse abroad? In several countries,\n spouse work rights exist — but this varies. We share current, country-specific\n information.\n12. How do I start? Book a free counselling session for a personalised nursing-career\n roadmap — no obligation.\n Compliance reminder: keep every answer free of job/visa/PR/salary guarantees."
