        "content": "8. FAQ (12)\n 1. Is respiratory therapy a good career abroad? Yes — especially in countries where it's\n a regulated profession (notably the USA and Canada, and in demand in the Gulf).\n 2. Is respiratory therapy recognised everywhere? No — in the UK and much of Europe,\n respiratory care is often handled by physios, nurses or clinical scientists. We help you\n target countries where the role formally exists.\n\n 3. What do respiratory therapists earn abroad? It varies widely; our table shows\n illustrative averages and is most meaningful where the profession is defined. We share\n realistic figures in counselling.\n 4. What licensing do I need to practise? Typically the country's credential/registration\n — e.g., NBRC (USA), CBRC (Canada), or Gulf health-authority licensing — plus an\n English test. We guide you.\n 5. Can I settle abroad with my family? Several countries offer skilled-worker and\n dependent-visa pathways that can lead to settlement — subject to eligibility and\n current rules. No guarantees.\n 6. What's the difference between these courses? BRT is the core respiratory-therapy\n degree; the others focus on cardiopulmonary diagnostics, sleep science, critical-care\n technology, or anesthesia & respiratory technology. We help you choose.\n 7. Which country should I aim for? Usually one where respiratory therapy is recognised\n and in demand — we advise honestly based on your goals.\n 8. Is critical-care / anesthesia technology a separate career? Yes — these are\n specialised allied-health technologist roles; recognition and licensing vary by country.\n 9. Is English mandatory? For most overseas licensing, yes — IELTS or OET. Academic\n Yatra offers prep.\n10. Do you guarantee a job, visa, or licence? No — be cautious of anyone who does. We\n provide honest, organised, end-to-end guidance.\n11. What are the eligibility requirements? Typically Class 12 with Science (PCB) +\n English and a minimum aggregate; specifics vary by course/country. We confirm for\n you.\n12. How do I start? Book a free counselling session for a personalised respiratory-care\n roadmap — no obligation.\n Compliance reminder: keep every answer free of job/visa/PR/salary/licence guarantees;\n be honest about country-by-country recognition."
