        "content": "SECTION 3 — MEDICAL LAB SCIENTIST SALARY ACROSS 10 COUNTRIES (flagship)\nHeading: What do medical lab scientists earn abroad?\nIntro: Below is an illustrative comparison of indicative average annual salaries for qualified\nmedical laboratory scientists / biomedical scientists (approx., in USD) across ten countries.\nUse it to explore possibilities — not as a promise.\n ⚠️ BANNER (must appear above table): Figures are illustrative & approximate, for\n qualified lab scientists/biomedical scientists. They vary widely by experience, role\n (clinical vs research), city, currency and year. Earning these requires meeting each\n\n country's registration and immigration requirements. These figures are fresh estimates\n (not from the Home page comparison) — verify with official sources before\n publishing/relying on them.\n\n Country Indicative average lab-scientist salary (USD/yr, approx.)\n\n 🇺🇸 USA ~$60,000\n\n 🇨🇦 Canada ~$55,000\n\n 🇦🇺 Australia ~$55,000\n\n 🇳🇴 Norway ~$50,000\n\n 🇩🇰 Denmark ~$48,000\n\n 🇩🇪 Germany ~$45,000\n\n 🇮🇪 Ireland ~$45,000\n\n 🇸🇪 Sweden ~$42,000\n\n 🇳🇱 Netherlands ~$42,000\n\n 🇬🇧 UK ~$38,000\n\n\n\n Role note: Research, molecular/genomics and biotech-industry roles can pay\n differently from routine clinical-diagnostic roles — and senior/specialist positions earn\n more. We share realistic, role-specific figures in counselling.\n Dev/content instructions: These are fresh illustrative estimates — replace every\n figure with a verified, dated number from a credible source (official labour-statistics,\n NHS/AfC bands for UK biomedical scientists, etc.) and add a \"Source & year\" line. Keep\n one currency (USD); consider a local-currency toggle. Keep the ⚠️ banner visible.\nHonest framing (below table):\n These are possibilities for qualified lab scientists, not guarantees. For clinical-diagnostic\n roles you'll typically need the country's registration (see Section 8) and an English test\n (IELTS/OET), plus meet visa rules. Research/industry roles often follow a different\n (licence-free) route. We help you plan whichever path fits you.\nCTA: Plan my lab-science career abroad →"
