        "title": "8. FAQ (12)",
        "content": "8. FAQ (12)\n 1. Is medical lab science a good career abroad? Yes — it's essential to healthcare, in\n demand, and offers both clinical-diagnostic and research/industry routes.\n 2. What's the difference between BMLS, BMLT and Biomedical Science? They\n overlap; BMLS/BMLT focus on clinical lab science/technology, while Biomedical\n Science can lead to clinical or research roles. We help you choose.\n\n 3. Can I work abroad without clinical registration? Often yes — research,\n molecular/genomics and biotech-industry roles usually don't need clinical\n registration, just the qualification and a work visa.\n 4. What registration do I need for clinical lab roles? Commonly ASCP (USA), HCPC as\n a Biomedical Scientist (UK), or CSMLS (Canada), plus English. We guide you.\n 5. What is the UK IBMS-accreditation point? For HCPC registration as a Biomedical\n Scientist in the UK, your degree usually needs to be IBMS-accredited — so if UK\n clinical work is your goal, choose an accredited programme. We flag this.\n 6. What do lab scientists earn abroad? It varies widely; our table shows illustrative\n estimates. Research/specialist roles differ. We share realistic figures in counselling.\n 7. Can I settle abroad with my family? Several countries offer skilled-worker and\n dependent-visa pathways that can lead to settlement — subject to eligibility and\n current rules. No guarantees.\n 8. What is Molecular Biology & Genetics good for? Research, genomics, molecular\n diagnostics and biotech — a fast-growing, future-facing field.\n 9. Is English mandatory? For most overseas registration and many roles, yes — IELTS or\n OET. Academic Yatra offers prep.\n10. Do you guarantee a job, visa, or registration? No — be cautious of anyone who does.\n We provide honest, organised, end-to-end guidance.\n11. What are the eligibility requirements? Typically Class 12 with Science (PCB) +\n English and a minimum aggregate; specifics vary by course/country. We confirm for\n you.\n12. How do I start? Book a free counselling session for a personalised lab-science\n roadmap — no obligation.\n Compliance reminder: keep every answer free of job/visa/PR/salary/registration\n guarantees; clearly separate clinical vs research routes and flag accreditation."
