        "title": "8. FAQ (12)",
        "content": "8. FAQ (12)\n 1. Is anaesthesia/OT technology a good career abroad? Yes — it's specialised and in\n demand, especially where roles are formally recognised (e.g., USA, UK, Gulf). Role\n titles and pay vary, so destination matters.\n 2. Is \"Anaesthesia Assistant\" the same as \"Anaesthesia Technologist\"? Not\n necessarily. In some countries an \"assistant/associate\" is an advanced, regulated role\n (e.g., US Anesthesiologist Assistant — master's + NCCAA; UK Anaesthesia Associate\n — GMC-regulated), distinct from a technologist role. We explain the difference\n clearly.\n 3. What is a Perfusionist? A specialised professional who operates the heart-lung\n machine during cardiac surgery — an advanced, certified, in-demand role.\n 4. What's an ODP? Operating Department Practitioner — a UK HCPC-registered\n perioperative profession across anaesthetics, surgery and recovery.\n 5. What do these roles earn abroad? Technologist roles earn moderately (see our\n illustrative table); advanced roles (US AA, perfusionist) pay much more. We share\n realistic, role-specific figures in counselling.\n 6. What certification do I need abroad? It depends on the role/country — e.g., NCCAA,\n CST, ABCP (USA); HCPC, GMC (UK); Gulf health-authority licensing. Plus English.\n We guide you.\n 7. Can I settle abroad with my family? Several countries offer skilled-worker and\n dependent-visa pathways that can lead to settlement — subject to eligibility and\n current rules. No guarantees.\n 8. Which country should I aim for? One where your target role is recognised and in\n demand — we advise honestly based on your goals.\n 9. Is English mandatory? For most overseas certification/registration, yes — IELTS or\n OET. Academic Yatra offers prep.\n10. Do you guarantee a job, visa, or certification? No — be cautious of anyone who does.\n We provide honest, organised, end-to-end guidance.\n\n11. What are the eligibility requirements? Typically Class 12 with Science (PCB) +\n English and a minimum aggregate; advanced roles may need a prior degree. We\n confirm for you.\n12. How do I start? Book a free counselling session for a personalised perioperative-\n career roadmap — no obligation.\n Compliance reminder: keep every answer free of job/visa/PR/salary/certification\n guarantees; be honest about role/title/recognition variation by country."
