        "title": "8. FAQ (12)",
        "content": "8. FAQ (12)\n 1. Is optometry a good career abroad? Yes — eye-care demand is rising globally, and\n optometrists are respected, well-paid clinicians where the profession is recognised.\n 2. What's the difference between B.Optom and Doctor of Optometry (OD)? B.Optom\n is a bachelor's degree; the OD is a professional doctorate required to practise as an\n optometrist in the USA (and used in some countries). We help you choose for your\n target country.\n 3. Can foreign-trained optometrists practise abroad? Often, but with significant\n requirements — e.g., USA needs an OD + NBEO + state licensure (foreign-trained may\n need to complete an OD/advanced standing); UK uses GOC; Australia uses\n AHPRA/OCANZ. We guide you honestly.\n 4. What are orthoptics and dispensing optics? Orthoptics treats eye-\n movement/binocular-vision disorders (UK: HCPC-registered); dispensing optics is\n fitting/supplying spectacles & lenses (UK: GOC-registered). Both are distinct eye-care\n roles.\n 5. What do optometrists earn abroad? It varies widely; our table shows illustrative\n averages. Optical/technician roles earn less. We share realistic figures in counselling.\n 6. Can I settle abroad with my family? Several countries offer skilled-worker and\n dependent-visa pathways that can lead to settlement — subject to eligibility and\n current rules. No guarantees.\n 7. Which country should I aim for? One where your target role is recognised and the\n degree level matches — we advise honestly.\n 8. Is Vision Science different from Optometry? Yes — Vision Science is more\n research/industry-oriented, while optometry is clinical practice. We help you choose.\n 9. Is English mandatory? For most overseas registration, yes — IELTS or OET.\n Academic Yatra offers prep.\n10. Do you guarantee a job, visa, or registration? No — be cautious of anyone who does.\n We provide honest, organised, end-to-end guidance.\n11. What are the eligibility requirements? Typically Class 12 with Science (PCB) +\n English and a minimum aggregate; specifics vary by course/country. We confirm for\n you.\n12. How do I start? Book a free counselling session for a personalised eye-care roadmap\n — no obligation.\n\n Compliance reminder: keep every answer free of job/visa/PR/salary/registration\n guarantees; be honest about degree-level and country-by-country recognition."
