        "content": "SECTION 4 — SALARY ACROSS 10 COUNTRIES (illustrative — fresh set)\nHeading: What do public-health & healthcare-management professionals earn abroad?\nIntro: Below is an illustrative comparison of indicative average annual salaries (approx., in\nUSD) across ten countries — blended for early-career public-health and healthcare-\nmanagement roles. Senior/specialist roles can pay significantly more.\n ⚠️ BANNER (must appear above table): Figures are illustrative & approximate,\n blended for public-health & healthcare-management roles. They vary widely by role,\n sector (govt/NGO/private/health-tech), seniority, city, currency and year. Earning these\n requires meeting each country's employment and immigration requirements. Verify\n with official sources before relying on them.\n\n Country Indicative average (public health & healthcare mgmt, USD/yr, approx.)\n\n 🇺🇸 USA ~$85,000\n\n 🇨🇦 Canada ~$75,000\n\n 🇦🇺 Australia ~$75,000\n\n 🇳🇴 Norway ~$65,000\n\n 🇩🇰 Denmark ~$62,000\n\n 🇮🇪 Ireland ~$60,000\n\n 🇩🇪 Germany ~$58,000\n\n 🇳🇱 Netherlands ~$58,000\n\n 🇬🇧 UK ~$55,000\n\n 🇸🇪 Sweden ~$52,000\n\n\n\n Role note: Healthcare administrators in large hospitals/insurers and senior public-\n health leaders can earn well above the figures above. Entry-level NGO/government\n roles can be lower. We share realistic, role-specific figures in counselling.\n ⚠️ Extra-verify note: These figures are a fresh illustrative set (not in the Home page's\n 6-profession table). Source & date them carefully before publishing.\n\n Dev/content instructions: Replace every figure with a verified, dated number; add a\n \"Source & year\" line. Keep one currency (USD); consider a local-currency toggle. Keep\n the ⚠️ banner + notes visible.\nHonest framing (below table):\n These are possibilities, not guarantees. You'll need the qualification and a valid work\n visa to take up roles — but there's no clinical-licensing exam to clear. We help you plan\n it.\nCTA: Plan my public-health / management career abroad →"
