        "content": "SECTION 3 — THE HONEST REALITY (key clarity)\nHeading: Read this first — PA is country-specific & competitive\nWe will not oversell this path. The truth:\n The PA role exists in select countries. USA, UK (Physician Associate), Canada (varies\n by province), Australia (limited/emerging in some states). Many countries don't have\n an equivalent role.\n Education is local + accredited. USA PA requires an ARC-PA-accredited master's\n programme + PANCE + state licensure. UK Physician Associate requires a UK PA\n\n master's + GMC registration (regulated from 2024).\n Admissions are highly competitive. PA programmes typically expect strong\n academics + relevant healthcare experience hours (often 1,000–2,000+ in the USA).\n Indian applicants need to plan for this.\n You usually can't transfer an Indian PA credential. The realistic route is to study the\n PA programme in your target country — not import a credential.\n Long, demanding programme. 2–3 years master's-level + supervised clinical hours.\n Honest framing: If PA in the USA/UK is your goal, we'll guide you realistically —\n including alternative healthcare careers (Nursing, Pharmacy, Public Health, MBBS\n abroad) if PA admission proves difficult."
